# Supply-chain guard: only resolve package versions published at least 7 days
# ago, so a hijacked release is usually caught and unpublished before it can
# land here. npm turns this into a rolling --before date. Enforced by recent
# npm 11 (checked on 11.10 and 11.13); npm 10 and 11.6 silently ignore it.
#
# npm ci and a plain npm install still honour package-lock.json as-is; this
# only gates new resolution (npm install <pkg>, npm update).
#
# Urgent security patch newer than 7 days? Override for that one install:
#   npm install <pkg>@<version> --min-release-age=0
min-release-age=7
